From swkaruri at insightful.com  Thu Mar 27 17:50:46 2008
From: swkaruri at insightful.com (Stella Karuri)
Date: Thu, 27 Mar 2008 10:50:46 -0700
Subject: Re: Help with mixed logistic model ( beta-binomial)
In-Reply-To: <825A13A34899AB40A5039B9E1B71939F01DE3160@HC-MAIL12.healthcare.uiowa.edu>
References: <825A13A34899AB40A5039B9E1B71939F01DE3160@HC-MAIL12.healthcare.uiowa.edu>
Message-ID: <96C6A984FE81AF4492020E9281CE67A8012C661A@sewinexch00.insightful.com>

The following will give you a data frame
with fitted values and grouping

 

fit1 <-glmmPQL(fixed =
any~FIRST.SE, random = 1|PROVUSRD, …)

fitVal <-fitted(fit1,levels=unique(DATA$PROVUSRD))

grouped.fit <-
data.frame(id=names(fitVal), fitVal)

 

or if you want the fitted values in lists
with each list corresponding to a center then try

 

fit1 <-glmmPQL(fixed =
any~FIRST.SE, random = 1|PROVUSRD, …)

fitVal <-fitted(fit1,levels=unique(DATA$PROVUSRD),
asList=T)

 

 

Stella

 

 

